a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 70vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 62 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx89gr9y/d3265b8a-2f70-4b9a-984a-053a3b8c99cd/41323270-5e0c-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx89gr9z.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>There are four sp<sup>2</sup>-carbon atoms, four sp<sup>2</sup>-nitrogen atoms and\nfour sp<sup>2</sup>-oxygen atoms as shown in structures I and II.</p>\n<p>Therefore, total number of atoms having sp<sup>2</sup>-hybridisation are\ntwelve (12).</p>"
